On 11/24/05 3:32 AM, Rami Lehti wrote:
> [S]queezing past boulders breaks Sokoban rules. And you get punished
> for it. Even though you get no message. I think you should get a
> message. At least the first time you break Sokoban rules.

I don't know. The whole handling of luck in the game is pretty much 
silent. The only time I can think of that you actually see an indication 
of a luck change in in-game messages is getting four-leaf clovers from 
sacrifices. Sometimes you see an effect of luck in the terms "luckily" 
or "unluckily" applied to an event. But there's no suggestion of luck in 
messages like "The unicorn gratefully accepts your gift," or "The mirror 
shatters!" I think that Sokoban handling its particular luck penalties 
silently is consistent with how luck is treated in the rest of Nethack.

